{"name":"End of Summer","hex":"#cc8f15","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"end","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ende."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The terminal point of something in space or time.","Share of joint responsibility."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/end"},{"term":"summer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of four seasons, traditionally the second, marked by the longest and typically hottest days of the year due to the inclination of the Earth and thermal lag. Typically regarded as spanning  either the period between the summer solstice to the autumnal equinox, or the months of June, July, and August in the Northern Hemisphere and the months of December, January and February in the Southern Hemisphere.","year; used to give the age of a person, usually a young one."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend the summer, as in a particular place on holiday."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summer"}],"entries":[{"title":"The End of Summer","blocks":[{"text":"The End of Summer  is a 1961 Japanese film directed by Yasujirō Ozu for Toho Films. It was entered into the 12th Berlin International Film Festival. The film was his penultimate; only An Autumn Afternoon (1962) followed it, which he made for Shochiku Films."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/09/The_End_of_Summer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_End_of_Summer","wikidata":"Q2476199"},{"title":"End of Summer (1995 film)","blocks":[{"text":"End of Summer is a 1995 American romantic drama film directed by Linda Yellen. It stars Jacqueline Bisset and Peter Weller and was first broadcast on Showtime. It received a limited theatrical release in 1997."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/End_of_Summer_(1995_film)","wikidata":"Q5375850"},{"title":"End of Summer (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"End Of Summer\" is a song by Tame Impala, the musical project of the Australian multi-instrumentalist Kevin Parker. It was released through Columbia Records on 25 July 2025, as the lead single from the project's fifth studio album, Deadbeat. Written and produced by Parker, the song was his first solo release in five years and his debut under Columbia."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1f/End_of_Summer_-_Tame_Impala.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/End_of_Summer_(song)","wikidata":"Q135675520"},{"title":"Summer","blocks":[{"text":"Summer or summertime is the hottest and brightest of the four temperate seasons, occurring after spring and before autumn. Starting on the summer solstice, daylight hours are the longest and darkness hours are the shortest, with day length decreasing as the season progresses after the solstice. In the Northern Hemisphere, summer is usually defined as starting on June 21 or 22, and ending on September 22 or 23; and in the Southern Hemisphere, as the period between December 22 or 23 and March 20 or 21."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Field_Hamois_Belgium_Luc_Viatour.jpg/330px-Field_Hamois_Belgium_Luc_Viatour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summer","wikidata":"Q1313"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Inari%2C_Finland_-_panoramio_%285%29.jpg/500px-Inari%2C_Finland_-_panoramio_%285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Inari%2C_Finland_-_panoramio_%285%29.jpg/1280px-Inari%2C_Finland_-_panoramio_%285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Inari%2C_Finland_-_panoramio_%28